TEXT 96 32 Left 3 ;PWM7805 33 - ORDINARY 1% REFERENCE DIVIDER; shared duty and direct dead-time thresholds
TEXT 96 80 Left 2 ;33 PCB positions:16 fixed R +7 C +5 IC packages +1 diode +3 pot bodies +1 selector header. Test loads/connectors excluded.
TEXT 96 544 Left 2 ;5 V / PASSIVE MIDPOINT AND ENDPOINT LIMITS
TEXT 896 192 Left 2 ;TRIANGLE / FREQUENCY POT
TEXT 96 1328 Left 2 ;DUTY INPUT / SHARED CMD
TEXT 96 1776 Left 2 ;ONE DUAL-GANG DEAD-TIME POT
TEXT 1408 1024 Left 2 ;LOW THRESHOLD / OUT1
TEXT 1408 1808 Left 2 ;HIGH THRESHOLD / OUT2
TEXT 96 2960 Left 2 ;ENDPOINT HANDLING USING EXISTING IC SECTIONS
TEXT 96 3360 Left 2 ;LOCAL BYPASS
TEXT 96 3744 Left 1 ;SEPARATE TRIAL: the original PWM7805 is unchanged. The endpoint limits follow the actual regulator rail; fixed5V accuracy across rail tolerances is not qualified.
TEXT 96 3792 Left 1 ;U1A is the LOWER endpoint detector, reusing the former midpoint buffer. U1B remains the triangle integrator. ONE TLC072CP DIP8.
TEXT 96 3840 Left 1 ;OSC+PA are ONE LM319N DIP14. PB+END_HIGH are the SECOND LM319N DIP14; all four comparator sections now used.
TEXT 96 3888 Left 1 ;END_HIGH collector shares PA directly: upper endpoint forces OUT1 high. BAT85 anodePB/cathodeFORCE_LOW: lower endpoint forces OUT2 high.
TEXT 96 3936 Left 1 ;U5A/C/D:ONE SN74ACT240N DIP20. Clock input2/output18. OUT1 inputs6/8/11, outputs14/12/9 in parallel.
TEXT 96 3984 Left 1 ;OUT2 inputs13/15/17, outputs7/5/3 in parallel. Spare input4=GND/output16 open. OE1/OE19=GND,VCC20=V5,GND10=0.
TEXT 96 4032 Left 1 ;CMD mixes COMMAND andVM. LOW/HIGH mix CMD with opposed dead-pot tracks. TRI<LOW:OUT1 high; LOW<TRI<HIGH:both low; TRI>HIGH:OUT2 high.
TEXT 96 4080 Left 1 ;This trims both edges. Ideal duties D-d and1-D-d, clipped; small pulses may vanish. It differs from the original rising-edge-only delay.
TEXT 96 4128 Left 1 ;PF:ONE single-gang50k linear frequency pot. PDT_H/L:ONE dual-gang1k dead pot. PD:ONE single-gang1k duty pot. No resistor arrays.
TEXT 96 4176 Left 1 ;REG:L7805CV TO220 pin1=IN,pin2=GND/tab,pin3=OUT. RM1/RM2=105ohm 1%; RMH/RML=9.76ohm 1%. Ladder draws about21.8mA. No added parts; all fixed resistors may be ordinary1%.
TEXT 96 4224 Left 1 ;Nominal models only: original TI amplifier family/ST comparator/Nexperia BAT85 models. ACT240/regulator functional assumptions retained. No full hardware/PVT or PCB-fit certification.
TEXT 96 4272 Left 1 ;Endpoint guard band widened to tolerate1% reference/duty resistors; outputs clamp earlier near0/5V. Op-amp saturation recovery and comparator offsets need bench checks. External command checked only near-0.1..5.1V.
TEXT 96 4320 Left 1 ;SOURCE1=external VD,SOURCE0=DP pot. FP0~20kHz/FP1~100kHz. DTP0..1~0..10%T. The maximum gap is approximate and frequency-dependent propagation remains.
TEXT 96 4368 Left 1 ;One transient:probe TRI,CMD,LOW,HIGH,OUT1,OUT2 directly. No saved plots. RLA/RSA/RLB/RSB and CLA/CLB are simulator test loads, not PCB parts.
TEXT 1408 3472 Left 1 !.include TLC074_TI.lib
TEXT 1408 3512 Left 1 !.include LM319_ST.lib
TEXT 1408 3552 Left 1 !.include L7805_Functional.lib
TEXT 1408 3592 Left 1 !.include ACT240_Functional.lib
TEXT 1408 3632 Left 1 !.include Symmetric_Parts.lib
TEXT 1408 3672 Left 1 !.include BAT85_Nexperia.lib
TEXT 1408 3712 Left 1 !.param FP=1 DP=.5 DTP=1 SOURCE=1 VD=2.5 VIN=8.5 LOAD=1 DRV_CORNER=0 REG_VSET=5 REG_DROP=2
TEXT 1408 3752 Left 1 !.options plotwinsize=0 threads=1 method=gear reltol=.003 solver=normal gmin=1e-9 abstol=1e-9 vntol=1e-5
TEXT 1408 3792 Left 1 !.tran 0 600u 0 20n uic
TEXT 96 128 Left 2 ;1% DIVIDER REVISION - only RM1/RM2 changed100->105ohm. Original file preserved. Other model/transition limits remain.
TEXT 96 4416 Left 1 ;PRE-EXISTING LIMITS:command-step overlap, zero-DT transitions and fixed5V external-input accuracy over regulator corners remain unqualified.
